  "verbalization": "Tioguanine is linked to Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a series of indications that suggest a potential role in the treatment of this condition. The evidence shows that Tioguanine is associated with Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia, which in turn is linked to Decitabine and Ivosidenib, both of which are indicated for Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia. This suggests that Tioguanine may have a role in the treatment of this leukemia subtype, possibly through a mechanism that involves the use of related drugs like Decitabine and Ivosidenib. The shared indication pathways imply a possible overlap in therapeutic targets or mechanisms, although the exact relationship remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential repurposing of Tioguanine for Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, but further research is needed to clarify the specific mechanism and clinical relevance.",
